losing tag before embedding; the closing tag literal is escaped to prevent prompt-structure breakage if a fallow finding's file path or message contains the sequence.\n796\t    SAFE_FALLOW_JSON=$(sed 's#</structural_findings>#<\\/structural_findings>#g' \"$FALLOW_EMBED_PATH\")\n797\t    STRUCTURAL_FINDINGS_BLOCK=$(printf '<structural_findings>\\n%s\\n</structural_findings>\\n' \"$SAFE_FALLOW_JSON\")\n798\t  else\n799\t    echo \"Warning: skipping structural findings embed (${FALLOW_JSON_SIZE} bytes > ${MAX_FINDINGS_SIZE} bytes). Re-run with narrower scope/profile if needed.\"\n800\t  fi\n801\tfi\n802\t```\n803\t\n804\tGather the capability review rules addressed to this reviewer (#4790): active `contribution` hooks with `into: code-reviewer`,\n805\tread from the loop point the review step is registered at (`workflow.code_review_point`, default `execute:post`). This is\n806\tadvisory by construction: any failure leaves the prompt without them and never blocks the review. The fragments are handed over once,\n807\tbelow, beside — never instead of — `${AGENT_SKILLS_REVIEWER}`:\n808\t```bash\n809\tREVIEWER_POINT=$(gsd_run query config-get workflow.code_review_point --raw 2>/dev/null) || REVIEWER_POINT=\"execute:post\"\n810\tcase \"$REVIEWER_POINT\" in execute:post|execute:wave:post) ;; *) REVIEWER_POINT=\"execute:post\" ;; esac\n811\tREVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON=$(gsd_run loop render-hooks \"${REVIEWER_POINT}\" --raw 2>/dev/null) || REVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON=\"\"\n812\tif [[ \"$REVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON\" == @file:* ]]; then REVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON=$(cat \"${REVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON#@file:}\" 2>/dev/null || true); fi\n813\t# A literal closing tag inside a fragment is escaped so third-party text cannot end the block early.\n814\tREVIEWER_CONTRIBUTIONS=$(printf '%s' \"$REVIEWER_HOOKS_JSON\" | node -e 'let s=\"\";process.stdin.on(\"data\",d=>s+=d).on(\"end\",()=>{try{const h=(JSON.parse(s).activeHooks||[]).filter(x=>x&&x.kind===\"contribution\"&&x.into===\"code-reviewer\"&&x.fragment&&typeof x.fragment.inline===\"string\"&&x.fragment.inline!==\"\").map(x=>x.fragment.inline.split(\"</capability_review_rules>\").join(\"<\\\\/capability_review_rules>\"));if(h.length)process.stdout.write(\"<capability_review_rules>\\n\"+h.join(\"\\n\\n\")+\"\\n</capability_review_rules>\")}catch(e){}})' 2>/dev/null || true)\n815\t```\n816\t\n817\tSpawn the gsd-code-reviewer agent:\n818\t\n819\tPrint: `◆ Spawning code reviewer... (runs in a subagent — no output until it returns, ~1–5 min; expected, not a freeze)`\n820\t\n821\t<!-- #2508 runtime-aware-dispatch -->\n822\t\n823\t> **Runtime-aware dispatch (#2508 Phase 4).** GSD workflows dispatch specialized subagents by role. Before dispatching on a built-in-only runtime (kimi-code — three built-ins only), resolve the role to a built-in via `gsd_run query resolve-dispatch-type --requested <role> --raw`. On named-dispatch runtimes (Claude/OpenCode/…) the role is returned unchanged; on kimi-code it maps to `coder`/`explore`/`plan` by role-suffix. The persona rides `${AGENT_SKILLS_<ROLE>}` (Phase 3) regardless. See @gsd-core/references/runtime-aware-dispatch.md.\n824\t\n825\t<!-- #2517 model-omit-on-inherit -->\n826\t\n827\t> **Model omission (#2517).** Omit the `model` parameter entirely when the value it would carry (`REVIEWER_MODEL`) is `\"inherit\"` or empty. An empty value 404s on runtimes without native tier aliases — the default on non-Claude runtimes. Omitting it inherits the orchestrator's model. See @gsd-core/references/model-profile-resolution.md.\n828\t\n829\t```\n830\tAgent(subagent_type=\"gsd-code-reviewer\", model=\"{REVIEWER_MODEL}\", prompt=\"\n831\t<required_reading>\n832\t${FILES_TO_READ}\n833\t</required_reading>\n834\t\n835\t${STRUCTURAL_FINDINGS_BLOCK}\n836\t\n837\t${EXTERNAL_EVIDENCE_BLOCK}\n838\t\n839\t<config>\n840\tdepth: ${REVIEW_DEPTH}\n841\tphase_dir: ${PHASE_DIR}\n842\treview_path: ${REVIEW_PATH}\n843\t${DIFF_BASE:+diff_base: ${DIFF_BASE}}\n844\tfiles:\n845\t${CONFIG_FILES}\n846\t</config>\n847\t\n848\tReview t