ked and unignored and appears in no commit (REVIEW WR-09).\n154\t- REQUIREMENTS, ROADMAP success criteria and PLAN truths agree on 30/120/300 and BUDGET-01. VALIDATION's `created`\n155\t  change (2026-09-28 to 2026-11-02) is in 4d1bd1a as the review said.\n156\t- Commit trail 8ddef7a, 4d1bd1a, 8a03c38, d230b4e, f633cf0 match the documents' references.\n157\t\n158\t## Not established\n159\t\n160\t- Whether the 90 s failover and 240 s pager figures are true of anything; they exist only in the plan.\n161\t- Who the \"operator\" in UAT line 18 is, or whether that decision was made at all; no source in the repo.\n162\t- The \"DevFlow resume instruction\" and the \"standing global instruction\" cited as authority in SUMMARY / VERIFICATION.\n163\t- Review claims that depend on runs I did not repeat: gitleaks results, \"12 of 15 mutants killed\", the generalist pass's\n164\t  Critical rating.\n165\t- Remote PR/release state beyond `git ls-remote origin` (`gh pr list` returned nothing and I did not confirm it\n166\t  authenticated, so I make no claim from it).\n167\t- Clock correctness: I compared the documents' timestamps with git commit dates, not with a trusted time source.\n168\t\n169\t##### security\n170\t\n171\t# Phase 01 security / leaked-data pass\n172\t\n173\t## Warnings\n174\t\n175\t### WR-01: Runtime files are not ignored by anything that travels with a clone; `git add .planning` stages one today and would stage both on a clone\n176\t\n177\t**Files:** `.gitignore:1-4`, `.planning/state.json` (untracked), `.planning/milestone.lock` (ignored only via `.git/info/exclude:7`)\n178\t\n179\t**Verified:**\n180\t- `git add -n .planning` in the worktree prints `add '.planning/state.json'`. `git add -n -A .` does the same.\n181\t- `git check-ignore -v` attributes `.planning/milestone.lock` to `.git/info/exclude`, which is not versioned. `.gsd/` is hidden only by its own self-ignoring `.gsd/.gitignore` (`*`), which is untracked and ignored, so it is also not in the repo.\n182\t- Negative control: in a scratch clone of `feature/phase-01` with both files copied into `.planning/`, `git add -n .planning` printed both `milestone.lock` and `state.json`.\n183\t- Content: `state.json` is a GSD command hint plus a timestamp, with no secrets. `milestone.lock` holds a Claude Code session id, a PID and an epoch timestamp (I did not print the values). `.gsd/dispatch-isolation-sentinel.json` has only isolation, phase, plan and timestamp fields.\n184\t\n185\t**Impact:** Neither file is tracked now, so nothing has leaked. A routine `git add .planning` or `git add -A` by a GSD step, an operator or a fresh clone would publish a session id and a PID in a PR. Both files are rewritten on every GSD action, so one stray commit would also add churn on every later phase.\n186\t\n187\t**Fix:** Add these to the tracked `.gitignore`:\n188\t```\n189\t.planning/state.json\n190\t.planning/milestone.lock\n191\t.gsd/\n192\t```\n193\tOr deliberately track `state.json`, but never the lock.\n194\t\n195\t## Info\n196\t\n197\t### IN-01: Stale claim in tracked 01-REVIEW.md\n198\t\n199\t**File:** `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-REVIEW.md:56`\n200\t**Issue:** The file says `gitleaks git --redact` scanned \"10 commits\". There are 12 commits in `main..HEAD` and 13 in the full history. The conclusion (no leaks) still holds (see below), but the figure is stale and it records no scan of the final tip.\n201\t**Fix:** Update the count, or drop it from the prose.\n202\t\n203\t## Checked and clean (with limits)\n204\t\n205\t- `gitleaks git --redact --log-opts=\"main..HEAD\"`: 12 commits, no leaks. `gitleaks git --redact` on the full history: 13 commits, no leaks. `gitleaks dir --redact .`: no leaks. gitleaks is installed at `/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin/gitleaks`. I ran no gitleaks negative control. The rg planted-sample control below is my only proof that a scanner can fire.\n206\t- Independent `rg` pass over the working tree (excluding `.git`) and over `git log -p main..HEAD`